[#
  The newest known version of each managed language that has one: the top of its CI version
  list, which tests every minor from the repo's version floor up to it. The values live in
  includes/toolchain-versions.json, one object per language keyed by its `languages` id, so
  shell reads them with `jq -r .go.newest includes/toolchain-versions.json` and never parses
  Jinja. This file only decodes them for the templates, which import
    [% from 'includes/toolchain-versions.jinja' import newest %]
  and get `newest`, e.g. newest.python == "3.14". Both files sit outside template/, so Copier
  never renders them.

  TypeScript and Rust have no entry: TypeScript tests the one Node LTS major the repo picks
  (node_version), and Rust builds with the repo's pinned toolchain (rust_toolchain).

  Raise Go only after the central golangci-lint pin is built with that Go and released:
  golangci-lint can't lint code for a Go newer than the one it was built with (ADR 0004).

  The JSON is read as a Jinja template before it is decoded, so it must hold no `[[`, `[%` or
  `[#` (no nested arrays).
#]
[% set _raw %][% include 'includes/toolchain-versions.json' %][% endset %]
[% set newest = {} %]
[% for lang, v in (_raw | from_json).items() %]
[% if v.newest is defined %]
[% set _ = newest.update({lang: v.newest}) %]
[% endif %]
[% endfor %]
